findings.finding:
α shifty ⇔ α divides x^k+x^l in ℤ[x,x⁻¹] ⇔ α=±x^p·g, g monic divisor of 1+x^d.  
g = product of cyclotomic Φ_{2m} with all m sharing same v₂(m).  
List Φ_{2m} (deg≤8):  
e=0:{x+1, x²−x+1, x⁴−x³+x²−x+1, x⁶−x⁵+…+1, x⁶−x³+1, x⁸+x⁷−x⁵−x⁴−x³+x+1}  
e=1:{x²+1, x⁴−x²+1, x⁸−x⁶+x⁴−x²+1}  
e=2:{x⁴+1, x⁸−x⁴+1}  
e=3:{x⁸+1}.  
Take any subset within one e, product g (deg≤8). 22 distinct g (incl. 1).  
For each g, p∈[0,8−deg(g)], sign ± gives 2·(9−deg(g)) α.  
Total α = Σ_g 2·(9−deg(g)) = 160.   (Pitfall: ensure same v₂, avoid mixing groups.)
